<title>UK: Nationwide B/S sets 150 mln stg FRN.</title>
<headline>Nationwide B/S sets 150 mln stg FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following fungible floating-rate issue was announced by lead manager HSBC Markets.</p>
<p> BORROWER   NATIONWIDE BUILDING SOCIETY</p>
<p> AMT ** 150 MLN STG   SPREAD   * FLAT	MATURITY	 AUG.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 BASE	 3M LIBOR  PAY DATE    03.OCT.96</p>
<p> LAST MOODY A1	  ISS PRICE  99.85     FULL FEES   15 BP</p>
<p> NOTES   ** FUNGLIBLE WITH 150 MLN STG FRN LAUNCHED JULY 31</p>
<p>	    * FIRST COUPON FIXED AT 5.8125 PCT</p>
<p> LISTING    LONDON    DENOMS (K) 100	 SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  UK	  TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    5 BP	SELL CONC  10 BP     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	FUNGIBLE FROM NOVEMBER 22</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
